VALUES (NULL, (SELECT id FROM topics WHERE name = $q$Advanced Financial Accounting and Reporting$q$ LIMIT 1), $q$If the acquisition-date fair value of identifiable net assets exceeds the consideration transferred plus the recognized amount of non-controlling interest, what should the acquirer do after reassessment?$q$, $q$multiple_choice$q$, $j$[{"label": "A", "text": "Recognize goodwill", "is_correct": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "Recognize a bargain purchase gain", "is_correct": true}, {"label": "C", "text": "Defer the difference in equity", "is_correct": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "Record the difference as other comprehensive income", "is_correct": false}]$j$::jsonb, $q$B$q$, $q$After reassessing the measurements, an excess of net identifiable assets over the acquisition-date amounts produces a bargain purchase gain. Goodwill arises from the opposite relationship.$q$, NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, $q$medium$q$, $q$"any excess of the net identifiable assets over the consideration transferred and NCI is recognized as a gain"

