VALUES (NULL, (SELECT id FROM topics WHERE name = $q$Advanced Financial Accounting and Reporting$q$ LIMIT 1), $q$In a downstream intercompany inventory sale from parent to subsidiary, the unrealized profit adjustment generally affects which party's reported profit?$q$, $q$multiple_choice$q$, $j$[{"label": "A", "text": "The parent's profit", "is_correct": true}, {"label": "B", "text": "The subsidiary's profit", "is_correct": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "Only NCI", "is_correct": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "Neither entity's profit", "is_correct": false}]$j$::jsonb, $q$A$q$, $q$In a downstream sale, the parent is the seller. The unrealized profit therefore originated in the parent's income and is eliminated against the parent's profit.$q$, NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, $q$medium$q$, $q$"downstream transactions are transactions from parent to subsidiary"

