VALUES (NULL, (SELECT id FROM topics WHERE name = $q$Auditing Theory$q$ LIMIT 1), $q$A major customer suffers a fire after year-end, creating a significant effect on the client’s financial statements. What treatment is generally appropriate?$q$, $q$multiple_choice$q$, $j$[{"label": "A", "text": "Ignore the event", "is_correct": false}, {"label": "B", "text": "Adverse opinion in every case", "is_correct": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "Disclosure if the condition arose after period end", "is_correct": true}, {"label": "D", "text": "Automatic adjustment for the fire itself", "is_correct": false}]$j$::jsonb, $q$C$q$, $q$A$q$, NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, $q$medium$q$, $q$"The PDF’s subsequent-event framework distinguishes conditions arising after period end as disclosure events rather than adjustment events. The exact reporting consequence depends on materiality and disclosure."

