VALUES (NULL, (SELECT id FROM topics WHERE name = $q$Auditing Practice$q$ LIMIT 1), $q$A vendor shipment under FOB destination was invoiced and recorded as a 2025 purchase even though it was received in January. Which procedure is appropriate?$q$, $q$multiple_choice$q$, $j$[{"label": "A", "text": "A. Inspect the freight terms and receiving report to determine whether the purchase should be deferred", "is_correct": true}, {"label": "B", "text": "B. Confirm the client's dividends", "is_correct": false}, {"label": "C", "text": "C. Recalculate equity investment gains", "is_correct": false}, {"label": "D", "text": "D. Count treasury shares", "is_correct": false}]$j$::jsonb, $q$A$q$, $q$The file describes a destination shipment received after year-end but recorded before year-end, so the auditor should test the purchase cutoff using terms and receipt evidence.$q$, NULL, NULL, NULL, FALSE, $q$hard$q$, $q$"Goods valued at P8,600 shipped by a vendor under FOB destination term, were received on January 3, 2026, and thus were not included in the physical inventory. Because the related invoice was received on December 31, 2025, this shipment was recorded as a purchase in 2025."

